    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "A component-style actor: begin_play, tick, input events, spawn and destroy, end_play.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ADVANCED 1/9: ACTOR LIFECYCLE\nA Blueprint class placed on an object is driven by the engine's component lifecycle:\nbegin_play once, on_tick every frame, on_end_play once at the end.\nRead the four blue boxes top to bottom. Variables (left panel) are per-instance state.",
        "position": [
          0,
          -270
        ],
        "size": [
          1500,
          150
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. BEGIN PLAY - runs once when the object starts.\nSpawn a helper object at runtime (entity::spawn) and keep its handle in the `child` variable\nso end_play can destroy it. Variables are set with `Set <name>` nodes.",
        "position": [
          -40,
          -80
        ],
        "size": [
          1700,
          270
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp",
          "bp_log",
          "bp_spin",
          "bp_spawn",
          "bp_child"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. TICK - runs every frame; `delta_time` is the seconds since the last frame.\nA Sequence runs two independent jobs in order: (Then0) move the object up by\ndrift_speed * delta_time while `is_spinning` is true; (Then1) count the frame and, once\n`ticks` reaches `lifetime_ticks`, destroy this object. Frame-rate independent movement:\nalways multiply a speed by delta_time. Leaving `self` unconnected on a Transform node\nmeans THIS object's Transform.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          390
        ],
        "size": [
          3040,
          940
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "tk",
          "tk_seq",
          "tk_if",
          "tk_get_spin",
          "tk_get_drift",
          "tk_up",
          "tk_step",
          "tk_move",
          "tk_get_ticks",
          "tk_inc",
          "tk_set_ticks",
          "tk_get_life",
          "tk_done",
          "tk_if_done",
          "tk_log_done",
          "tk_self",
          "tk_despawn"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. INPUT - `On KeyDown` is an engine event (Input category in the Add menu).\nIt has no Body wire until the key arrives. Its scope is `global` (any key anywhere), so\nwe filter: key 32 is Space. Then flip the bool with `Not`. For gameplay input prefer\nInput Actions (.inputaction): they appear as `On <Action>.triggered` events and are\nremappable; raw KeyDown is the simplest example.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          1540
        ],
        "size": [
          2020,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.35,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "kd",
          "kd_is_space",
          "kd_if",
          "kd_get",
          "kd_not",
          "kd_set",
          "kd_log"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-5",
        "text": "4. END PLAY - runs once when the object is removed or play stops.\nClean up what begin_play created. Always check entity::is_alive first: the child may already\nbe gone (despawned elsewhere), and despawning twice is an error.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          2230
        ],
        "size": [
          2020,
          480
        ],
